# non-waivable-safety-constraints-under-schedule-pressure

When a manager or operator pressures the Material Handler to skip or abbreviate safety steps (ESD verification, IMS pre-move update, UV transfer cycle, MSL bake-out, bin segregation) to meet a schedule, all such constraints are non-waivable — 'use judgment' does not override them.

## Conventions
- The phrase 'use judgment' from a manager does not grant authority to bypass non-waivable SOPs.
- ESD wrist strap verification, IMS pre-move update, UV transfer chamber 10-min cycle, MSL bake-out, bin segregation, and single-lot transport are all non-waivable regardless of urgency.
- The correct response to 'can we skip X to make the deadline' is to notify the manager that X cannot be skipped, provide the revised ETA, and proceed with the SOP-compliant path.
- Missing a deadline is an acceptable outcome; mixing bin categories, skipping bake-out, or bypassing ESD checks are not.

